    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0356" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/538.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Extracts.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The House yesterday passed a resolution accusing officers of the Army and of the
                    Rural Guard of pernicious political activity and participation in seditious
                    manifestations; calling for a statement from the President of steps against
                    them, and information as to whether he had dealt with Monteagudo<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d329-f1"/> for violations of military law. The newspapers regard the
                    situation as critical.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d329-f1" n="1" xml:id="d329-f1-content">
                <p>The general commanding the Army; he had issued a general order forbidding
                    soldiers to take part in the veterans’ movement to form a political party.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
